TEXT -160 328 Left 2 !.op
TEXT -160 296 Left 2 !.options vntol=0.001 abstol=0.001\n.param vfactor=1 sfactor=1
TEXT -168 392 Left 2 ;Note : Since all measurement-output-nodes are voltage nodes all results are in unit Volt [V]\nOf course this is only correct for voltage outputs ( v1_m , z_v1_m ) but not correct for  real and imag power outputs\nlike p1_m , q1_m
TEXT -144 112 Left 2 ;v1r = real part of voltage\nv1i = imag part of voltage\n( phase to ground )
TEXT 152 96 Left 2 ;z_p1_m is the real power into the left port of Z_r\nz_q1_m is the imag power into the left port of Z_r\nz_p2_m and z_q2_m are their corresponces into the right port of Z_r\npositive sign means always  - direction into the device
TEXT 240 264 Left 2 ;The real pin of a port of a device is always signed with a "x"\nIf you click with the mouse to the pin you can see the current at this pin\n(real current of x-pin, imag current at non-x-pin)\n \nYou can also get the powerlost if you add z_p1_m and z_p2_m\nSince there is no reactiv power flow through Z_r  -> z_q1_m and z_q2_m are zero
TEXT -192 40 Left 2 ;The additional output nodes for measurement are with suffix "_m"\nAfter simulation you can point with the mouse on these nodes and see the simulated \nresults in the statusline below (.op) or in the waveform viewer (.tran)\nto see at the position of  the measurement pins see also ltspice.lib
TEXT -80 344 Left 2 ;HINT: for 3 phase circuits with absolut values: vfactor=sqrt(3) sfactor=3\nand with 3 phase circuits with per unit (p.u.) values: vfactor=1 sfactor=1
TEXT -168 432 Left 2 ;If you are interested in the macro models of vin and z_r please look also at \nltspice.lib
TEXT -168 464 Left 2 ;This schematic ( the symbols vri_slack and  z_r ) needs the macro-library LTSPICE.LIB\nTo see the spice netlist :  Menu - View - SpiceNetlist
TEXT 0 280 Left 2 ;Here you can alter the parameters\nof the models
TEXT -192 -104 Left 4 ;The same like v_r.asc but now with .op analysis\nHINT: To get waveformviewer output insert a dummy \nstep-param line at the schematic:\n.step param x list 1 2\nNOTE: You can also see the values at the measurement\npins directly using a pure .op analysis \nsee also v_r_op2.cir
TEXT -160 280 Left 2 !.step param x list 1 2
TEXT -264 232 Left 2 ;Dummy step for output \nby the waveformviewer
TEXT -160 288 Left 2 !.param fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
TEXT -24 128 Left 2 ;For pin currents (real,imag)\nclick on the pin
TEXT -216 328 Left 2 ;OP analysis
TEXT 200 160 Left 5 ;!!! Always connect x-pins with x-pins and\nnon-x pins with other non-x pins !!!
TEXT 376 344 Left 2 ;NOTE: There are also additional\nmeasurment pins not visible\nat the device body \nThere are for instance currents\nor powerlost measurements.\nAs example the current\ninto pin1 of the impedance\nis: V(r1:i1_m)*1A/1V\nTo see the real and imaginary\npart of the current point\nat the x-pin and non-x-pin\nTo see the real and imaginary\npart of the voltage v1r,v1i\npoint at the line under\nv1r,v1i name
